Give an array of more than 10 000 values its values in the start function.

V8 refuses an `array.new_fixed` of more values than 10 000
(`kV8MaxWasmArrayNewFixedLength`), and a constant expression has no other way
to give an array values that differ. So a defining global whose array is
longer, and mutable, is made empty, `array.new_default` or, for an element type
with no default, an `array.new` of its first value; and the start function
copies the values in, with `array.init_data` from a passive data segment for
numbers, or `array.init_elem` from a passive element segment for references,
then drops the segment. An element segment's items are constant expressions
read after every global, so they can name any defining global, cycles
included. The fill is kept with its defining global, and every application of
state puts the fills of the globals it keeps back in the start function.

The defining globals an application allocates while serializing a partially
evalled ctor's locals, before the globals are applied, are now kept by that
application: they were dropped as the previous application's, and the code
that resumes the ctor read a global that no longer existed.

